20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klein</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Schoenborn</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><publisher-name>National Center for Health Statistics</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Hyattsville (MD)</publisher-loc><source>Age adjustment using the 2000 projected U.S. population. Healthy People Statistical Notes no. 20</source></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="book"><source>Bridged-race vintage 2002 postcensal population estimates for July 1, 2000&#x02013;July 1, 2002, by year, county, single-year of age, bridged-race, Hispanic origin, and sex</source><year>2003</year><publisher-loc>Hyattsville (MD)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>National Center for Health Statistics</publisher-name><comment>Available from:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.cdc.gov/nchs/about/major/dvs/popbridge/datadoc.htm#vintage2002">http://www.cdc.gov/nchs/about/major/dvs/popbridge/datadoc.htm#vintage2002</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Keppel</surname><given-names>KG</given-names></name><name><surname>Pearcy</surname><given-names>JN</given-names></name><name><surname>Klein</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><publisher-loc>Hyattsville (MD)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>National Center for Health Statistics</publisher-name><source>Measuring progress in healthy people 2010. Statistical Notes no. 25</source></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="book"><year>2002</year><publisher-loc>Chicago (IL)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>SPSS Inc</publisher-name><source>SPSS Base 11.5 User's Guide</source></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Owings</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><issue>329</issue><year>2002</year><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>18</lpage><article-title>2000 National Hospital Discharge Survey</article-title><source>Adv Data</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12664934</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="book"><year>2001</year><publisher-loc>Austin (TX)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Texas Health Care Information Council</publisher-name><source>Texas hospital inpatient discharge public use data file 2000</source></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="book"><source>Patient Discharge Frequencies for California 2003 [database on the Internet]</source><publisher-loc>Sacramento (CA)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Office of Statewide Health Planning and Development, Healthcare Quality &#x00026; Analysis Division</publisher-name><year>2003</year><comment>Available from:<ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://oshpd.ca.gov/hqad/PatientLevel/Frequencies/1FrequenciesAtoK.htm#Statewide%20Totals">http://oshpd.ca.gov/hqad/PatientLevel/Frequencies/1FrequenciesAtoK.htm#Statewide%20Totals</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="book"><publisher-name>Bureau of Public Health Statistics</publisher-name> <year>2000</year><publisher-loc>Phoenix (AZ)</publisher-loc><source>Arizona hospital discharge summary reports, 2000</source></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Warner</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><publisher-loc>San Diego, California</publisher-loc><source>Health and medical care in San Diego and Tijuana: prospects for collaboration. Briefing paper prepared for the San Diego Dialogue's Forum Fronteriz